ween Rollo Bjorn and  lagertha in which Rollo tries to claim  paternity over Bjorn only to be rejected  in favor of his brother yet again  I've heard something to that effect but  for truth  having played the character with this  moment in mine standin was pleased with  how it turned out saying I felt  rewarding to come back and actually  purge all that stuff that I had in the  previous seasons just as the Vikings  believed a life after death for their  heroes many TV shows never dispatched  their most beloved characters for good  fans of the show's old guard are hoping  that Rollo might make another return  during the final season of Vikings and  Hearst has dropped a confusing hint  that's giving them hope when asked by  cinema bland whether Rollo might show up  in season 6 first answered cryptically I  would say yes and no but rolos  reappearance will be a huge surprise as  indeed it was rather a surprise to me  but I'll leave it to that I don't want  to be too evasive but the answer in the  long-term is both yes and no he may be  referring to the history the show is  loosely based on although if the  showrunner is surprised by his own plots  fans have little chance of predicting  this one even if Rollo doesn't make it  back to Vikings for the final season we  may not have seen the last of the  character we already know that a  spin-off series is in the works with  Netflix Vikings ball Hollow will be set  to century after Vikings and will center  around William the Conqueror in  real-life William was the first Norman  King of England just as Rollo was the  first Viking king of Normandy that's not  the only connection between the two  series William was actually a descendant  of Rollo  even though Rollo will be long dead by  the beginning of Vikings Valhalla his  dreams of ultimate power will finally  come to fruition to his family line  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite stuff or coming soon  subscribe 